KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12 --unwind 2 --unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ one digit: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
unwinding assertion loop \d+: FAILURE
--
libc++ formats an integer with vsnprintf (num_put::__do_put_integral).  The
C library model of vsnprintf writes a nondeterministic string, so the
loops over its result in num_put and __pad_and_output have no bound
smaller than the buffer, and symbolic execution of `os << 7' does not
terminate in practice (cpp11_stream_setw and
cpp11_ostream_integer_insertion_classic_locale time out on macOS).  With
libstdc++, which formats integers itself, the program verifies in 8 s.
